A host key press waits in the Dana's backlog while Palm OS's key queue (8 keys of 7 bytes) could overflow, counting the presses already in the FIFO, so a fast burst into a slow app (the memo key's editor) isn't dropped. A release of a key that is down goes ahead of a waiting press, a press that wakes the ST always goes in, and the queue is only read from RAM. Unblocking is seen when the backlog is next fed (a report read or CycleSlowly); an app that never reads keys lets presses build up to the 8192 backlog instead of being dropped.

